  * xattention.py
        <- minference/modules/xattention.py
  * xattn_utils.py
        <- minference/ops/op_utils/xattn_utils.py

Local modifications (see each file header):
  - xattention.py: the cross-module import of the two Triton helpers
    (`from ..ops.xattention_fa import flat_group_gemm_fuse_reshape,
    softmax_fuse_block_sum`) is repointed to the co-vendored `xattn_utils`,
    where those functions are actually DEFINED. Upstream `xattention_fa` only
    re-exported them while also importing the heavy
    `pit_sparse_flash_attention_v3` / `vertical_slash_utils` chain that the
    `Xattention_prefill` entry never calls — vendoring two files instead of five
    keeps the footprint minimal and self-contained (xattn_utils imports only
    torch + triton).
  - xattn_utils.py: vendored whole, reformatted to repo style (black/isort),
    logic unchanged (header note only).

No algorithmic change was made: the block-selection (`find_blocks_chunked`), the
strided estimate (`xattn_estimate`), and the `block_sparse_attn`-backed prefill
(`Xattention_prefill`) keep their exact upstream behavior; the vendored files
were reformatted to this repo's style (black/isort, line length 99) with logic
unchanged. Numerics match flash dense on a real Qwen3-8B layer (rel ~0.0005 @
threshold=0.98, verified in this environment). The selected-block attention runs
on `block_sparse_attn` (the same kernel Stem uses); head_dim 256 is gated to the
torch reference because block_sparse_attn miscomputes at 256.

